[
  {
    "file": "robot-walk-rejected-v1.png",
    "mode": "built-in image_gen",
    "prompt": "Use case: identity-preserve. Edit target is the provided existing robot walk sheet. Produce corrected FOUR-frame 2x2 transparent sprite sheet, same painted turquoise tin robot, gold winding key, yellow smiling face, red gloves/boots, same proportions, right-facing three-quarter camera, scale and texture. Change ONLY walking poses. Frame A top left: NEAR leg swings to RIGHT (forward), FAR leg on LEFT (back), both grounded, arms normal walking opposite swing. Frame B top right: NEAR leg is planted upright under hip, FAR knee swings to RIGHT, far boot raised. Frame C bottom left: NEAR leg MUST extend visibly to LEFT (behind torso), FAR leg MUST extend visibly to RIGHT (forward support). The near knee and near boot in C must be on the LEFT side of the pelvis, absolutely opposite A. Do not depict near leg forward in C. Frame D bottom right: FAR leg planted under hip, NEAR knee swings to RIGHT crossing passing pose. Torso transfers weight subtly and keeps identical dimensions. Arms alternate normal gait, never point or punch. A-B-C-D-A loop. Frame A and C have visibly reversed near/far leg phases. Preserve style and components, no effects or text, no duplicated supports, no anatomy redesign, full transparent margin. Body ground anchors aligned.",
    "status": "Reprovado; não integrado."
  },
  {
    "file": "girl-low-crouch-v1.png",
    "mode": "built-in image_gen",
    "prompt": "Use case: identity-preserve. References 1 and 2 are the exact official game heroine standing and crouching, enlarged with nearest-neighbor solely for reference. Create a SINGLE new low defensive crouch sprite for this SAME small child. Preserve face, brown ponytail, bangs, cream and brown dress, brown shoes, warm limited colors, EXACT soft low-resolution painted/dithered game-sprite technique; no smooth cartoon redesign. Facing RIGHT three-quarter side view. She must crouch VERY LOW with bent knees tucked fully, torso folded forward over knees, head and ponytail lowered to almost knee level so the entire body silhouette is less than 40 percent of her standing height. Keep head width and bodily proportions by folding the pose, not shrinking or squashing the person. Hands near floor, visibly ducking under a horizontal attack, eyes glance right. Do NOT draw standing or merely kneeling upright; head is sideways and lowered, dress folds cover bent legs. Full natural parts, no sword, no beam, no effects, no text. One sprite, true transparent background with no background remnants, no cast shadow. Match reference identity and painting; no new costume, no changed age or palette.",
    "status": "Pose baixa utilizada somente na arena."
  },
  {
    "file": "train-body-v1.png",
    "mode": "built-in image_gen",
    "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Edit target: attached original painted toy locomotive, single game sprite. Preserve exact identity, painted texture, red cab, blue boiler, green wagon, proportions, perspective, palette, outlines and lighting. Change ONLY the visible red coupling rod and its two small gold eccentric crank pins: remove the connecting red rod and those protruding pins, reconstruct the underlying gold wheel surfaces naturally. Leave the ordinary round central hubs on each wheel. The same locomotive and all four complete wheels must remain, nothing else removed. No redesign, no extra objects, no ground shadow, no glows. Actual transparent background, entire train with generous transparent margin. This is a clean body layer to animate the original mechanical parts separately, not a new design.",
    "status": "Camada pintada utilizada na animação mecânica."
  }
]
